OVERVIEW: Convert between DICOM and XML formats

Converts DICOM files to XML format (Native DICOM Model, PS3.19 Annex A.1)
and vice versa, with bulk data handling. Every attribute is a DicomAttribute
with tag, vr and keyword; an attribute with an empty Value Field is kept
with no Value element (PS3.19 Table A.1.5-2).

Examples:
  dicom-xml file.dcm --output file.xml
  dicom-xml file.xml --output file.dcm --reverse
  dicom-xml file.dcm --pretty

USAGE: dicom-xml <input> [--output <output>] [--reverse] [--pretty] [--no-keywords] [--include-empty] [--no-include-empty] [--inline-threshold <inline-threshold>] [--bulk-data-url <bulk-data-url>] [--metadata-only] [--filter-tag <filter-tag> ...] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <input>                 Input file (DICOM or XML)

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output file path
  -r, --reverse           Convert from XML to DICOM
  -p, --pretty            Pretty-print XML output
  --no-keywords           Deprecated: don't write the keyword attribute (the
                          output then breaks PS3.19 Table A.1.5-2, which
                          requires it for PS3.6 elements; will be removed)
  --include-empty/--no-include-empty
                          Keep attributes with an empty Value Field as a
                          DicomAttribute without Value (PS3.19 Table A.1.5-2)
                          (default: --include-empty)
  --inline-threshold <inline-threshold>
                          With --bulk-data-url: OB/OD/OF/OL/OV/OW/UN values
                          longer than this many bytes become BulkData (0: all
                          of them); without it every such value is InlineBinary
                          (PS3.19 Table A.1.5-2) (default: 1024)
  --bulk-data-url <bulk-data-url>
                          Base URL for BulkData uri values, <url>/<GGGGEEEE>,
                          inside items <url>/<SQ tag>/<item n>/<GGGGEEEE>
                          (PS3.19 Table A.1.5-2 reserves uri for a WADO-RS
                          Retrieve Metadata response)
  --metadata-only         Metadata only (PS3.18 10.4.1.1.2): leave out every
                          OB/OD/OF/OL/OV/OW/UN value at any depth (Pixel Data,
                          Float Pixel Data, Encapsulated Document, Waveform,
                          Overlay, LUTs); with --bulk-data-url each becomes
                          BulkData instead
  --filter-tag <filter-tag>
                          Keep only this attribute: PS3.6 keyword, GGGG,EEEE or
                          GGGGEEEE (can be used multiple times)
  --verbose               Verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

